12. BOOKING REFERENCES AND ORDER TRACKING
==================================================

Every booking must receive a unique, human-readable order reference.

Use a format such as:

CLS-20261023-0001

Generate references safely on the server or in the database to avoid collisions.

Every booking should store:
- Customer ID.
- Service ID.
- Service name snapshot.
- Selected options.
- Booking date.
- Order reference.
- Requested pickup date and time.
- Confirmed pickup details.
- Garment quantities or estimated weight.
- Customer instructions.
- Quoted price.
- Final price.
- Payment status.
- Order status.
- Created and updated timestamps.

Use the following order-status workflow:

1. Booking Received.
2. Awaiting Confirmation.
3. Pickup Scheduled.
4. Laundry Received.
5. Processing.
6. Ready for Collection.
7. Out for Delivery, if applicable.
8. Completed.
9. Cancelled.

Display the current status clearly in the customer dashboard.

Provide a simple visual order progress indicator on the order detail page.

Show timestamps for important status changes.

Only an authorized administrator should be able to update operational order statuses.

Do not automatically mark an order as completed because a customer opened WhatsApp.

Do not automatically mark an order as ready for collection without an authorized update.

Allow customers to request cancellation where the business permits it, but require the business to approve cancellation when necessary.

Maintain an order status history for auditing.

