23. SECURITY AND ACCESS CONTROL
==================================================

Security is mandatory.

Implement Supabase Row Level Security policies and appropriate server-side authorization.

CUSTOMER PERMISSIONS

Customers may:
- Read their own profile.
- Update permitted profile fields.
- Create their own bookings.
- Read their own bookings.
- Read their own notifications.
- Mark their own notifications as read.

Customers must not:
- Read another customer's profile.
- Read another customer's bookings.
- Read another customer's notifications.
- Change their role to administrator.
- Set unauthorized order statuses.
- Modify administrative settings.
- Edit prices or payment records outside permitted operations.

ADMINISTRATOR PERMISSIONS

Only authorized administrators may:
- View all bookings.
- Update operational order statuses.
- Manage customer records where authorized.
- Manage service categories and prices.
- Manage testimonials.
- Update business settings.
- Manage administrative data.

Assign administrator roles through a secure server-side process or trusted database administration process.

Never let public registration assign administrative privileges.

Do not rely solely on client-side route guards.

Keep privileged database keys and service-role credentials on the server.

Never expose secrets through NEXT_PUBLIC environment variables.

Validate all incoming data on the server.

Use safe database queries and proper error handling.

Protect authentication and administrative actions against unauthorized access.

